include "../../src/help/escalation.mlpl";
b={max_question_bytes:256,max_context_bytes:4096,max_source_bytes:512,max_transcript_bytes:512};
r=u:help_escalation_demo(b)?;
print("DEMO: progressive built-in sw-MLPL help and honest escalation");
print("Scenario: a tiny browser helper should answer grounded language questions cheaply, but it must not invent facts, diagnose without program evidence, inspect repositories it cannot access, or silently disclose code to a stronger model.");
print("Native boundary: MLPL owns request validation, typed routing, context minimization, and inert bundle construction. The six classifier/retrieval features are fixtures here; no model, browser, server, network call, or command execution is hidden behind the demo.");
print("Budgets: 256 question bytes; 512 source and transcript bytes each; 4096 encoded bundle bytes; six fixed requests; no automatic send and no automatic execution.");
print("Mechanics: each request arrives with classifier/retrieval/context features. MLPL validates its schema and budgets, then returns one typed outcome: Answer, NeedDocs, NeedProgramContext, NeedRepository, NeedReasoning, or OutsideDomain. The same contract can later receive scores from a learned router.");
print("Tiers: browser answers from current documentation; browser-index requests current knowledge; sw-mlpl-serve can add program/repository context; portable-external creates a user-controlled bundle for a stronger assistant.");
print("1. Grounded local answer — ordinary array help stays private and immediate:");
print({question: r.local.bundle.question,outcome: r.local.outcome,tier: r.local.tier,answer: r.local.answer.text,example: r.local.answer.example,citation: r.local.answer.citation,why: r.local.reason});
print("2. Program diagnosis — documentation alone cannot explain an observed rank. The bundle includes source only because consent_source=1:");
print({question: r.program.bundle.question,outcome: r.program.outcome,tier: r.program.tier,why: r.program.reason,include_source: r.program.bundle.include_source,source: r.program.bundle.source,runtime_error: r.program.bundle.runtime_error});
print("3. Implementation question — parser source/history requires repository-capable local help:");
print({question: r.repository.bundle.question,outcome: r.repository.outcome,tier: r.repository.tier,destination: r.repository.bundle.destination,why: r.repository.reason});
print("4. Broader reasoning — offer a portable external bundle, but withhold private source and transcript because neither was consented:");
print({question: r.reasoning.bundle.question,outcome: r.reasoning.outcome,tier: r.reasoning.tier,destination: r.reasoning.bundle.destination,why: r.reasoning.reason,include_source: r.reasoning.bundle.include_source,source: r.reasoning.bundle.source,include_transcript: r.reasoning.bundle.include_transcript,transcript: r.reasoning.bundle.transcript});
print("5. Version mismatch — a stale documentation hit is not treated as truth:");
print({question: r.docs.bundle.question,outcome: r.docs.outcome,tier: r.docs.tier,why: r.docs.reason});
print("6. Outside domain — progressive help declines rather than impersonating a general assistant:");
print({question: r.outside.bundle.question,outcome: r.outside.outcome,tier: r.outside.tier,why: r.outside.reason});
print("Outcome coverage [Answer, NeedDocs, NeedProgramContext, NeedRepository, NeedReasoning, OutsideDomain]:");
print(r.counts);
print("Interpretation: escalation is a deterministic capability and privacy decision, not a tiny model's conversational guess. Retrieval and interpreter evidence remain the truth layer; learned routing, Engram memory, semantic search, and answer composition can improve Tier 0 later without changing this boundary.");
ok(1)
